+# Coverage
+
+- Dock operating window: 05:30-17:30 PT, with Doors 3 and 4 reserved for the planned dispatch waves.
+- Opening lead: Talia.
+- Closing lead: Reece.
+- Talia: 05:30-14:00 PT.
+- Minh: 06:00-15:00 PT.
+- Reece: 08:00-17:00 PT.
+- Priya: remote, 09:00-17:00 PT.
+
+# Dispatch Schedule
+
+- Shared control: lock each wave's manifest 30 minutes before its pickup.
+- Wave 1 - Owner: Talia.
+- Wave 1 - Backup: Minh.
+- Wave 1 - Carrier/service: Redwood Ground.
+- Wave 1 - Staging deadline: 07:15 PT.
+- Wave 1 - Pickup: 08:00 PT.
+- Wave 1 - Volume: 220 orders.
+- Wave 1 - Destination mix: 140 Northern California / 80 Mountain.
+- Wave 1 - Door: use one of reserved Doors 3 and 4.
+- Wave 2 - Owner: Minh.
+- Wave 2 - Backup: Reece.
+- Wave 2 - Carrier/service: Redwood Ground.
+- Wave 2 - Staging deadline: 13:00 PT.
+- Wave 2 - Pickup: 14:00 PT.
+- Wave 2 - Volume: 160 orders.
+- Wave 2 - Destination mix: 90 Pacific Northwest / 70 Southwest.
+- Wave 2 - Door: use the other reserved door among Doors 3 and 4.
+
+# Exception Playbook
+
+- Scan hold: if outbound scan completion is below 98% at the staging deadline, hold the wave; the wave owner runs a 15-minute recount before release.
+- Carrier no-show: call the carrier desk within 10 minutes; if the recovery ETA exceeds 45 minutes, the backup owner opens overflow Door 5 and moves the staged freight there.
+- Volume surge: if actual order volume is at least 12% above the planned wave volume, Priya pulls the reserve-labor list and the wave owner opens packing Lane C.
+- Damage threshold: if damage exceptions exceed 5 cartons in a wave, pause the affected pallet and have Priya open an incident ticket before loading.
+
+# Communications
+
+- Primary channel: #reno-weekend-ops.
+- Opening update: post at 05:45 PT.
+- Pickup updates: post immediately after each pickup.
+- Closing update: post at 16:45 PT.
+- Update fields: report scan percentage, staged order count, current exception count, and carrier ETA.
+- Escalation chain: Talia, then Owen, then the Logistics Duty Manager.
